---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Who carries the video" hint="Up to 30 participants, each with a seeded uplink and downlink. Choose how the media travels, and see every client's upload and download, the server's bandwidth and CPU, which clients are overloaded, and how sharp the video is for the slow viewers.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>mesh</b> and 12 participants: every client must upload <b>11 copies</b> of its video, which needs 16.5 Mbit/s up. <b>All 12 are overloaded</b>, because even the best uplink in the room (8 Mbit/s) cannot carry it, and the slow viewers see about <b>222 kbit/s</b> per tile.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>SFU, one stream each</b>: every upload is one stream and the server does the copying (about <b>180 Mbit/s</b> out), but it cannot lower the quality for one viewer, so <b>8 of 12</b> clients are overloaded and the 6 slow viewers are <b>breaking up</b>.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>SFU with simulcast</b>: senders upload up to three layers and the server gives each viewer the layer that fits. <b>Nobody is overloaded</b>, and slow viewers get a steady <b>383 kbit/s</b> per tile. <b>MCU</b> also overloads nobody, but its server needs <b>4.8 cores</b> instead of 0.35, and the slow viewers get 273 kbit/s per tile, because one mosaic is shared by all the tiles.</li>
    <li>Raise participants to <b>30</b>: even simulcast leaves <b>10 clients overloaded</b>, because they must decode 29 streams (CPU) or cannot fit even 29 low layers (paused tiles). This is why big meetings show a page of tiles instead of everyone.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg vcb" data-vcb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Participants <input type="range" min="3" max="30" value="12" data-n /> <b data-nval></b></label>
      <label>How the media travels <select class="pg-in" data-topo>
        <option value="mesh">Mesh (everyone sends to everyone)</option>
        <option value="sfu" selected>SFU, one stream each</option>
        <option value="simulcast">SFU with simulcast layers</option>
        <option value="mcu">MCU (server mixes one picture)</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Server traffic</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Server CPU</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Overloaded clients</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Slow viewers (6 Mbit/s or less)</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="vcb-wrap" tabindex="0" role="table" aria-label="Every client: upload, download, picture quality and status">
      <div class="vcb-row vcb-head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">Client</span><span role="columnheader">Upload used / link</span><span role="columnheader">Download used / link</span><span role="columnheader">Picture per tile</span><span role="columnheader">Status</span></div>
      <div data-rows></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: the participants are drawn from a seeded list, with uplinks from 1 to 20 Mbit/s and downlinks from 3 to 100 Mbit/s, and everyone sees every other participant. A full stream is 1,500 kbit/s (720p), and simulcast layers are 150, 500 and 1,500 kbit/s, uploaded from the lowest up while they fit. In a <b>mesh</b> each link carries the least of 1,500, the sender's uplink divided by the other participants, and the viewer's downlink divided by them; 15% of pairs cannot connect directly and are relayed by a TURN server. A client is overloaded if it needs more than its link, or if its CPU (an encode costs 1 unit for 720p, 0.4 for 360p and 0.15 for 180p, and a decode costs 0.05 plus up to 0.25 by bitrate) goes above 8. In a plain <b>SFU</b> a viewer that cannot carry all the streams loses packets, so the picture breaks up. In <b>simulcast</b> each viewer splits its downlink evenly, and if even the 150 kbit/s layers do not fit, tiles are paused. An <b>MCU</b> decodes every stream and encodes one 3 Mbit/s mosaic per viewer, cut to the viewer's downlink, so per tile is the mosaic divided by the number of tiles. Server CPU: forwarding costs 1 core per Gbit/s plus 0.002 per forwarded stream, and the MCU costs 0.1 core per decode and 0.3 per encode.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style is:global>
  .vcb-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; }
  .vcb-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4.5rem minmax(9rem, 1fr) minmax(9rem, 1fr) minmax(9rem, 1fr) minmax(9rem, 1.2fr); gap: 4px 12px; padding: 5px 10px; min-width: 44rem; font: .8rem var(--font-mono); align-items: center; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .vcb-row[hidden] { display: none; }
  .vcb-head { border-top: 0; background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  .vcb-row.over { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bad) 10%, var(--surface)); }
  .vcb-row .st { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .vcb-row.over .st { color: var(--bad-text); }
  .vcb-bar { display: block; height: 5px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; margin-top: 2px; }
  .vcb-bar i { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); }
  .vcb-bar i.full { background: var(--bad); }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-vcb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    // ---- simulation (pure functions; the page only calls them) ----
    //#sim-start
    const H = 1500; const LAYERS = [150, 500, 1500]; const COMP = 3000; const MAXN = 30; const CPU_LIMIT = 8; const SLOW = 6000;
    const SEED = 11;
    const RELAY_RATE = 0.15; // share of pairs that cannot connect directly
    const DECODE = { base: 0.05, full: 0.25 }; // client CPU cores per tile: 0.05 plus up to 0.25 at full bitrate
    const ENCODE = { high: 1, mid: 0.4, low: 0.15 }; // simulcast encode cost per published layer, in cores
    const KBPS_PER_CORE = 1e6; // a server core forwards 1 Gbit/s
    const SFU_CORES_PER_STREAM = 0.002;
    const MCU_CORES = { decode: 0.1, encode: 0.3 }; // per participant
    const QUALITY = { sharp: 1000, good: 400, blurry: LAYERS[0] }; // kbit/s per tile for 720p, 360p, 180p
    const SERVER_CPU_BAD = 4;
    // linear congruential generator (Numerical Recipes constants)
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const UPS = [1000, 1500, 2500, 4000, 8000, 20000]; const UPW = [2, 3, 3, 3, 2, 1];
    const DOWNS = [3000, 6000, 12000, 30000, 100000]; const DOWNW = [2, 3, 3, 3, 2];
    const draw1 = (a: number[], w: number[]) => { let r = rnd() * w.reduce((x, y) => x + y, 0); for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) { r -= w[i]; if (r < 0) return a[i]; } return a[a.length - 1]; };
    const people = Array.from({ length: MAXN }, (_, id) => ({ id, up: draw1(UPS, UPW), down: draw1(DOWNS, DOWNW) }));
    const relay = Array.from({ length: MAXN }, () => Array.from({ length: MAXN }, () => rnd() < RELAY_RATE)); // pairs that cannot connect directly
    const dec = (k: number) => DECODE.base + DECODE.full * Math.min(1, k / H);
    const sum = (a: number[]) => a.reduce((x, y) => x + y, 0);
    type Client = { id: number; up: number; down: number; upNeed: number; upUse: number; downNeed: number; downUse: number; tiles: number[]; shown: number; cpu: number; avg: number; loss: boolean; reasons: string[] };
    function simulate(n: number, topo: string) {
      const m = n - 1;
      const c: Client[] = people.slice(0, n).map((p) => ({ ...p, upNeed: 0, upUse: 0, downNeed: 0, downUse: 0, tiles: [], shown: m, cpu: 0, avg: 0, loss: false, reasons: [] }));
      let ingress = 0; let egress = 0; let cpu = 0;
      if (topo === 'mesh') {
        let rel = 0;
        for (const a of c) {
          a.upNeed = m * H; a.downNeed = m * H; a.upUse = Math.min(a.upNeed, a.up);
          for (const s of c) if (s.id !== a.id) { const k = Math.min(H, s.up / m, a.down / m); a.tiles.push(k); if (relay[s.id][a.id]) rel += k; }
          a.downUse = sum(a.tiles); a.cpu = m + sum(a.tiles.map(dec));
          if (a.upNeed > a.up) a.reasons.push('needs more upload');
          if (a.downNeed > a.down) a.reasons.push('needs more download');
        }
        ingress = rel; egress = rel; cpu = rel / KBPS_PER_CORE;
      } else if (topo === 'sfu') {
        const s = c.map((a) => Math.min(H, a.up));
        for (const a of c) {
          a.upNeed = H; a.upUse = s[a.id];
          const tiles = c.filter((x) => x.id !== a.id).map((x) => s[x.id]); a.downNeed = sum(tiles);
          const f = Math.min(1, a.down / a.downNeed); a.tiles = tiles.map((k) => k * f); a.downUse = a.downNeed * f;
          a.cpu = 1 + sum(a.tiles.map(dec));
          if (a.downNeed > a.down) { a.loss = true; a.reasons.push('streams exceed the link'); }
        }
        ingress = sum(c.map((a) => a.upUse)); egress = sum(c.map((a) => a.downNeed)); cpu = egress / KBPS_PER_CORE + n * m * SFU_CORES_PER_STREAM;
      } else if (topo === 'simulcast') {
        const sent = c.map((a) => { const l: number[] = []; let u = 0; for (const x of LAYERS) if (u + x <= a.up) { l.push(x); u += x; } return l; });
        for (const a of c) {
          const pub = sent[a.id]; a.upNeed = sum(pub); a.upUse = a.upNeed;
          const enc = (pub.includes(LAYERS[2]) ? ENCODE.high : 0) + (pub.includes(LAYERS[1]) ? ENCODE.mid : 0) + ENCODE.low;
          const share = Math.floor(a.down / m);
          let tiles = c.filter((x) => x.id !== a.id).map((x) => { let p = sent[x.id][0]; for (const l of sent[x.id]) if (l <= share) p = l; return p; });
          a.downNeed = sum(tiles);
          if (a.downNeed > a.down) { a.shown = Math.floor(a.down / LAYERS[0]); tiles = tiles.slice(0, a.shown); a.reasons.push(`${m - a.shown} tiles paused`); }
          a.tiles = tiles; a.downUse = sum(tiles); a.cpu = enc + sum(tiles.map(dec));
        }
        ingress = sum(c.map((a) => a.upUse)); egress = sum(c.map((a) => a.downUse)); cpu = egress / KBPS_PER_CORE + n * m * SFU_CORES_PER_STREAM;
      } else {
        for (const a of c) {
          a.upNeed = H; a.upUse = Math.min(H, a.up); a.downNeed = COMP; a.downUse = Math.min(COMP, a.down);
          a.tiles = Array(m).fill(a.downUse / m); a.cpu = 1 + dec(H);
        }
        ingress = sum(c.map((a) => a.upUse)); egress = sum(c.map((a) => a.downUse)); cpu = n * MCU_CORES.decode + n * MCU_CORES.encode;
      }
      for (const a of c) {
        a.avg = a.tiles.length ? sum(a.tiles) / a.tiles.length : 0;
        if (a.cpu > CPU_LIMIT) a.reasons.push('CPU maxed');
      }
      return { c, ingress, egress, cpu };
    }
    //#sim-end
    const fmtK = (k: number) => (k >= 1000 ? `${(k / 1000).toFixed(k >= 10000 ? 0 : 1)} Mbit/s` : `${Math.round(k)} kbit/s`);
    const quality = (a: Client) => (a.loss ? 'breaking up' : a.avg >= QUALITY.sharp ? 'sharp 720p' : a.avg >= QUALITY.good ? 'good 360p' : a.avg >= QUALITY.blurry ? 'blurry 180p' : 'poor');
    const rowsEl = q('[data-rows]');
    const rows = Array.from({ length: MAXN }, () => {
      const el = document.createElement('div'); el.className = 'vcb-row'; el.setAttribute('role', 'row'); el.hidden = true;
      const cells = Array.from({ length: 5 }, () => { const s = document.createElement('span'); s.setAttribute('role', 'cell'); el.append(s); return s; });
      const bars = [1, 2].map((i) => { const b = document.createElement('span'); b.className = 'vcb-bar'; const f = document.createElement('i'); b.append(f); cells[i].append(document.createElement('span'), b); return f; });
      cells[4].className = 'st'; rowsEl.append(el);
      return { el, cells, bars };
    });
    const nodes = [1, 2, 3, 4].map((i) => ({ box: q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${i}]`), o: q(`[data-o${i}]`), n: q(`[data-n${i}]`) }));
    let frame = 0;
    function draw() {
      frame = 0;
      const n = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-n]').value); const topo = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-topo]').value;
      q('[data-nval]').textContent = String(n);
      const r = simulate(n, topo);
      rows.forEach((row, i) => {
        row.el.hidden = i >= n; if (i >= n) return;
        const a = r.c[i]; const over = a.reasons.length > 0;
        row.el.classList.toggle('over', over);
        row.cells[0].textContent = `#${i + 1}`;
        const pu = Math.min(1, a.upUse / a.up); const pd = Math.min(1, a.downUse / a.down);
        (row.cells[1].firstChild as HTMLElement).textContent = `${fmtK(a.upUse)} / ${fmtK(a.up)}`; row.bars[0].style.width = `${Math.round(pu * 100)}%`; row.bars[0].classList.toggle('full', a.upNeed > a.up);
        (row.cells[2].firstChild as HTMLElement).textContent = `${fmtK(a.downUse)} / ${fmtK(a.down)}`; row.bars[1].style.width = `${Math.round(pd * 100)}%`; row.bars[1].classList.toggle('full', a.downNeed > a.down);
        row.cells[3].textContent = `${fmtK(a.avg)}, ${quality(a)}`;
        row.cells[4].textContent = over ? a.reasons.join(', ') : 'ok';
      });
      const over = r.c.filter((a) => a.reasons.length > 0).length;
      const slow = r.c.filter((a) => a.down <= SLOW); const slowAvg = slow.length ? sum(slow.map((a) => a.avg)) / slow.length : 0;
      const slowBad = slow.filter((a) => a.loss).length;
      nodes[0].o.textContent = `in ${fmtK(r.ingress)}, out ${fmtK(r.egress)}`; nodes[0].n.textContent = topo === 'mesh' ? `only the relayed pairs (${RELAY_RATE * 100}%) go through a TURN server` : 'what the media server receives and sends';
      nodes[1].o.textContent = `${r.cpu.toFixed(2)} cores`; nodes[1].n.textContent = topo === 'mcu' ? 'decodes every stream and encodes a mosaic for every viewer' : topo === 'mesh' ? 'only relaying' : 'only copies packets, no decoding';
      nodes[2].o.textContent = `${over} of ${n}`; nodes[2].n.textContent = 'more demand than the link or the CPU can carry';
      nodes[3].o.textContent = slow.length ? `${fmtK(slowAvg)} per tile` : 'none in this meeting'; nodes[3].n.textContent = slow.length ? `${slow.length} viewers${slowBad ? `, ${slowBad} breaking up` : ''}` : '';
      nodes[0].box.style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)'); nodes[1].box.style.setProperty('--c', r.cpu > SERVER_CPU_BAD ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      nodes[2].box.style.setProperty('--c', over ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'); nodes[3].box.style.setProperty('--c', slowBad || slowAvg < QUALITY.blurry ? 'var(--bad)' : slowAvg >= QUALITY.good ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', over > 0);
      const msg: Record<string, string> = {
        mesh: `Mesh: every client uploads ${n - 1} copies, so ${over} of ${n} clients are overloaded. The server is almost idle, but the clients cannot carry the meeting. Mesh only works for two or three people.`,
        sfu: `SFU with one stream each: uploads are one stream, and the server copies it (${fmtK(r.egress)} out). It cannot lower quality for one viewer, so ${over} clients are overloaded and ${slowBad} of the slow viewers are breaking up.`,
        simulcast: `SFU with simulcast: each viewer receives the layer that fits, so ${over === 0 ? 'nobody is overloaded and slow viewers get a steady low layer' : `${over} clients are still overloaded, by CPU or paused tiles, so a big meeting must show only a page of tiles`}. Server CPU stays small at ${r.cpu.toFixed(2)} cores.`,
        mcu: `MCU: every client sends one stream and receives one mosaic, so nobody is overloaded. The price is on the server: ${r.cpu.toFixed(1)} cores to decode and encode, and a picture whose layout the viewer cannot choose.`,
      };
      out.textContent = msg[topo];
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(draw); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
